# German language (product copy)

User-facing German in this repo must be **grammatically correct and easy to understand**.
Applies to Builder **and** Synergien, and to docs guild members actually read.

## Scope

- UI labels, buttons, tooltips, toasts, errors, empty states, Erste Schritte
- `README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and any AGENTS / notes text that users see
- Strings in `src/builder-body.html`, `src/builder-app.js`, `src/synergien-source.html`
  (and rebuilt `index.html` / `synergien.html`)

Code comments and internal pipeline notes may stay mixed; **product surfaces stay German.**

## Tone: **du** (informal guild)

Address the player as **du** / **dein** — not **ihr** / **Sie**.
Stay consistent in every new string. Existing copy already uses du; do not introduce ihr.

## Clarity

- Prefer short, clear sentences over nested clauses.
- Avoid Anglizismen when a good German word fits (z. B. „Nachschlagewerk“ statt
  „Lookup“, „Vorschlag“ statt „Suggestion“ in UI).
- **OK as game terms:** Path, Build, Wildcard, Addon, Import, Export, Talent,
  Spell, Cooldown, Crit, Hit, und ähnliche Client-/Season-Begriffe.

## Grammar traps (do not ship)

- Broken compounds (`Build Schmiede` → Buildschmiede; Bindestriche nur wo nötig)
- Wrong articles / case (`der`/`die`/`das`, Genitiv, Präpositionen)
- **dass** vs **das**
- Dangling or mixed address (du in one line, ihr in the next)
- `text-transform: uppercase` on labels that may contain Umlaute — Chrome leaves
  ü/ä/ö lowercase (“Übernehmen”). No uppercase transform on such labels
  (see AGENTS.md Fallen → Umlaute)

## Both surfaces

Synergien is first-class with the Builder (`.cursor/rules/synergien-first-class.mdc`).
German quality rules apply equally to both; do not polish Builder copy and leave
Synergien broken.

## Do not mass-rewrite

Fix or write German for the change you are shipping. Full-repo copyedit is a
separate task — do not rewrite all strings “while here.”

Details also anchored in `AGENTS.md` (Regeln) and
`.cursor/rules/full-agent-utilization.mdc`.
